{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, דֵּךְ","hw":"דֵּךְ","html":"† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">דֵּךְ</span></big></big>  <strong>demonstr. pr. m. this</strong>, <strong>f.</strong> <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּךְ</span>; only Ezr; Dn uses <span dir=\"rtl\">דִּכֵּן</span> <strong>(</strong>Egyptian and Cappad. Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">זך</span> (CIS <sup>ii. 151</sup> RÉS <sup>361 B</sup> S-C<sup>Pap.</sup> (f. <span dir=\"rtl\">דכא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דכי</span> ib.<sup>F 6, 9</sup>), Lzb<sup>Eph. i. 67</sup>); 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">דֵּיכֵי</span>, f. <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּךְ</span>; Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">ذَاكَ</span>; Ethiopic ዝኩ From <span dir=\"rtl\">ذَا</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">זֶה</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּא</span> (f.), with the affix ך (W<sup>CG 110</sup>), thus lit. = Germ. <em>dieser da</em>. The pl. is <span dir=\"rtl\">אִלֵּךְ</span>, q.v.<strong>)</strong>;—<em>this</em> (always after its subst.), <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:16\" href=\"/Ezra.5.16\">Ezr 5:16</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">שֵׁשְׁבַּצַּר דֵּךְ</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:17\" href=\"/Ezra.5.17\">17</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">בֵּית־אֱלָהָא דֵךְ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:7\" href=\"/Ezra.6.7\">6:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:8\" href=\"/Ezra.6.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 6:12\" href=\"/Ezra.6.12\">12</a>; f. <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:13\" href=\"/Ezra.4.13\">4:13</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:15\" href=\"/Ezra.4.15\">15</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:16\" href=\"/Ezra.4.16\">16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:19\" href=\"/Ezra.4.19\">19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 4:21\" href=\"/Ezra.4.21\">21</a> all <span dir=\"rtl\">קִרְיְתָא דָךְ</span>, <a data-ref=\"Ezra 5:8\" href=\"/Ezra.5.8\">5:8</a>.","next":"BDB Aramaic, דִּכֵּן","prev":"BDB Aramaic, דִּינָיֵא"}